  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "Multi-agent systems (MAS) are computational architectures in which multiple autonomous agents\u2014each with their own perception, memory, and action capabilities\u2014interact within a shared environment to accomplish tasks that benefit from parallelisation, specialisation, or distributed coordination. In contemporary AI, MAS are realised through networks of LLM-backed agents orchestrated by frameworks that manage inter-agent communication, tool invocation, and task decomposition. Emergent collective behaviours, coordination protocols, and mechanism-design principles from classical MAS theory inform how modern agentic systems handle conflict, deception, and incentive alignment.",
